--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

llama.cpp — the inference engine IdleToken runs on. It is NOT vendored here:
    scripts/build_llamacpp.sh fetches the pinned upstream commit recorded in
    scripts/llamacpp-patches/UPSTREAM and builds it with the patches in that
    directory, so the source (and the licence that travels with it) comes from
    upstream. It is not linked into any IdleToken binary either — llama-server
    and the ggml rpc-server are spawned as separate processes. Those two
    executables ARE shipped inside the installers, and this notice covers that
    redistribution.
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
    MIT License — full text in the LICENSE file of the upstream checkout
    Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

Mbed TLS (v3.6.7) — the TLS implementation used by IdleToken's transport patch
    for the ggml RPC link. Not vendored here either: the patched llama.cpp
    build pulls it through CMake FetchContent and links it statically, so it is
    present in the llama-server and rpc-server executables shipped inside the
    installers.
    Copyright The Mbed TLS Contributors
    Apache License 2.0 — full text in the LICENSE file of the fetched source
    Upstream: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls

ds4 — the generic kernels of IdleToken's early prototype (ds4.c, plus the
    project's own ds4x layer). SHELVED since 2026-08-16 and NOT part of any
    build: the call sites are satisfied by src/common/ds4_stub.c, no ds4 object
    is compiled, and no released binary contains any of this code. The sources
    stay in the private tree for reference only and are not part of the public
    distribution. The MIT licence and copyright notice are reproduced anyway,
    in vendor/ds4/LICENSE, because the terms travel with the material we did
    take from upstream.
    Copyright (c) 2026 The ds4.c authors
    Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
    MIT License — full text in vendor/ds4/LICENSE
    Upstream: https://github.com/antirez/ds4 (pinned commit in vendor/ds4/UPSTREAM)

Rax (rax.c, rax.h, rax_malloc.h) — a radix tree implementation that ships
    inside the ds4 sources. It is reached only through the shelved ds4 path
    described above (IDLETOKEN_WITH_DS4=1), so it is neither distributed in
    source form nor present in any released binary. Listed here as history:
    it sits inside vendor/ds4/ but is NOT covered by that directory's MIT
    LICENSE, and if the ds4 path is ever built and redistributed again, the
    BSD 3-clause terms require this notice in binary form too.
    Copyright (c) 2017-2026, Salvatore Sanfilippo <antirez at gmail dot com>
    BSD 3-Clause — full text in the header of vendor/ds4/rax.c

